            <div xml:id="d659">

                <pb facs="0721" n="617" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg617"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/63: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-22T13:00:00+08:00">March 22, 1932—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 22—3:05 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>361. Following from Reuter, Tokyo, March 21st: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Acknowledging the Manchurian government’s note of March 12th but making
                            no reference to the question of recognition, the Japanese Government
                            today sent a communication through the Japanese Consul <pb facs="0722"
                                n="618" xml:id="pg618"/> at Changchun welcoming the new state’s
                            declared policy of the open door, equal opportunity and respect for
                            existing treaties.”</p></quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
